Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/content/pm/PackageInstaller.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
the Unity test APK resolve list, batch E: SessionInfo.getAppIcon asks the local installer for the session's icon.

Why: a session listed in bulk (getAllSessions, getMySessions) has no icon, and getAppIcon then asks the package
manager service for the session's own: AppGlobals.getPackageManager().getPackageInstaller(). Minato's
AppGlobals.getPackageManager() answers no IPackageManager (framework.jar leaves the interface out, ADR-0045), so the
call ended the app with NoClassDefFoundError. The app's sessions are LocalPackageInstaller's, which answers the same
lookup in the process; the result is the one Android gives, the session's icon, or null for a session without one.

--- a/core/java/android/content/pm/PackageInstaller.java
+++ b/core/java/android/content/pm/PackageInstaller.java
@@ -4050,13 +4050,8 @@
             if (appIcon == null) {
                 // Icon may have been omitted for calls that return bulk session
                 // lists, so try fetching the specific icon.
-                try {
-                    final SessionInfo info = AppGlobals.getPackageManager().getPackageInstaller()
-                            .getSessionInfo(sessionId);
-                    appIcon = (info != null) ? info.appIcon : null;
-                } catch (RemoteException e) {
-                    throw e.rethrowFromSystemServer();
-                }
+                final SessionInfo info = LocalPackageInstaller.sessionInfo(sessionId);
+                appIcon = (info != null) ? info.appIcon : null;
             }
             return appIcon;
         }
